meta {
  name: Save Answer
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/assessments/attempts/{{assessmentAttemptId}}/answers/{{assessmentQuestionId}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "response": { "selectedOptionIds": ["opt-1"] },
    "is_flagged": false,
    "time_spent_secs": 32
  }
}

docs {
  Upserts one answer (autosave — call again to overwrite). response shape
  depends on the question's response_format:
  - single_choice / multi_choice  -> { selectedOptionIds: string[] }
  - ranking / sequence            -> { order: string[] }
  - fill_blank_drag_drop /
    fill_blank_dropdown           -> { blankAnswers: { blankId, optionId }[] }
  - text_response                 -> { text: string }
  - audio_response                -> { audioUrl: string }  (Read Aloud,
    Repeat Sentence, Describe Image, Audio Speaking Response — upload the
    student's recording FIRST via the generic upload flow: POST
    /student/uploads/audio/presign -> PUT to uploadUrl -> POST
    /student/uploads/audio/verify -> use the returned permanentUrl here)

  Only the field(s) matching the question's own response_format are read;
  send exactly one populated field per call. Autoscorable question types
  are scored immediately (auto_score + evaluation_status: "auto_scored");
  audio_response and other non-autoscorable types always stay "pending"
  for evaluator scoring — there is no machine scoring path for audio at
  all, it's evaluator-reviewed 100% of the time.

  Requires the attempt to be "in_progress". response is itself optional —
  a student can flag a question or record time_spent_secs without having
  answered yet (at least one of response/is_flagged/time_spent_secs is
  required).
}
